===Etymology===
Modification of capital letter {{m|mul|B}} ([[File:UncialB-01.png|class=skin-invert-image|16px|Approximate form of upper case B when the loop was dropped to form lower case ''b'']]) by dropping its upper loop, from the Greek letter {{m|mul|Β||Beta}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|mul|Voiced bilabial plosive.ogg|Pronunciation of IPA {{IPAfont|[bɑː, ɑbbɑː]}} with the sound {{IPAfont|[b]}}}}
*: A [[voiced]] [[bilabial]] [[stop]] is made with the lips alone, by a complete closure cutting off all exit of breath from the mouth, but with accompanying sonant vibrations of the vocal chords, the current of air necessary to produce this being driven from the lungs into the closed cavity of the mouth.<ref>{{R:Century|year=1914}}</ref> The corresponding voiceless stop is {{m|mul|p}}.

===Letter===
{{letter|mul}}

# {{Latn-def|mul|letter|2}}
# Transliterates the Cyrillic letter [[б#Translingual|б]].

===Symbol===
{{mul-symbol}}

# {{lb|mul|IPA}} A [[voiced]] [[bilabial]] [[plosive]].
# {{lb|mul|superscript {{angbr IPA|ᵇ}}|IPA}} {{IPAfont|[b]}}-[[onset]] ([[prestopping]] / [[preocclusion]] / [[preplosion]]), {{IPAfont|[b]}}-[[release]] (e.g. {{angbr IPA|ɡᵇ}} for {{IPAfont|[ɡ͡b]}}), {{IPAfont|[b]}}-coloring, or a weak, fleeting or epenthetic {{IPAfont|[b]}}.
# {{lb|mul|particle}} A [[bottom quark]].
# {{lb|mul|music}} {{altform|mul|♭||flat}}

====Usage notes====
The letter {{m|mul|b}} is used in several romanization systems to represent the bilabial plosive or stop, usually voiced ({{IPAchar|/b/}}), including [[Cyrillic]] {{m|mul|б||be}}, [[w:Zhuyin fuhao|Zhuyin fuhao]] [[ㄅ]], and Korean jamo {{m|mul|ㅂ||bieup}}.

